--- !u!114 &4454183590977230711
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4407273690977191190}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c3e757e2d127424418697c7f630eae63, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Tutorial
  tutorialSteps:
  - NEW THREAT APPROACHING | Welcome to Level 2, the Coastal Reef. Water tiles block
    your ground towers, and enemy threats intensify. Watch out for Plastic Bombers
    entering the battlefield. They explode on impact, dealing heavy area-of-effect
    damage to your defenses.
  - 'SUPPORT TOWER: CRYSTAL SPRING | The pollution is intensifying on the shores.
    Build a Crystal Spring tower near the path. It sprays pure water to activate
    an AoE Slow mechanic, slowing down fast-moving toxic groups and giving your defensive
    units more time to strike.

'
  - 'HAZARD WARNING: OIL LIGHTERS | The enemy forces are pushing harder. Beware of
    Oil Lighters entering the fray. They will set active pollution puddles on fire,
    creating dangerous hazards that deal heavy damage-over-time to any units caught
    in the blaze.

'
  - 'MANAGE POLLUTION LEVELS | Do not give up ground to the corruption. You must
    use your Cleanse mechanics to reduce the water pollution levels before they max
    out. Keep the contamination meter down at all costs, or it is Game Over.

'
  - 'BOSS WAVE: OIL BEHEMOTH | Warning. The final wave of this biome is here and
    the Oil Behemoth boss has arrived. This massive ground threat leaves a sticky
    oil trail that accelerates enemy movement and explodes with massive area damage
    upon death. Concentrate all your fire to bring it down.

'
  tutorialHeaderTMPText: {fileID: 5044308140966489782}
  tutorialBodyTMPText: {fileID: 5697766486235210383}
  tutorialImages:
  - {fileID: 9209111032081802488}
  - {fileID: 5978599424980311321}
  - {fileID: 1246302348806925061}
